## Implemented Control Surface

| Area | Implemented behavior |
| --- | --- |
| Catalogue | 1,966 taxonomy leaves, 1,738 chart kinds and 246 native families; 81 stock documents in light and dark themes. |
| Grammar | 17 transforms, 24 layouts, 18 marks, 20 encoding channels, 7 coordinates and 15 scales through canonical chart inference. |
| Authoring | Named tables and scales, groups, ordering, clipping, per-layer and per-mark styles, guides, captions and physical typography. |
| Customization | Reversible chart mutations, semantic diffs, explicit missing/null handling and atomic array edits. |
| Rendering | Shared resolved primitives produce plans, scenes and TikZ; native families compose with numerical layers. |
| Execution | Actual Bun, Chromium and Node workers provide progress and cancellation, owned font transport and closed results. |
| Validation | Neutral JSON/Gherkin contracts; independent D3, AJV, Canvas, PDF.js and Python oracles; native compilation and bounded raster inspection. |
| Developer routes | Bun/Nx through existing script routers and grouped launch/seed registrations. |

The product README documents the canonical authoring flow. Current registered generation refreshes the83 existing catalogue/reference artifacts; Source-derived metadata reports77 physical native packages,169 public commands,4237 scoped key occurrences and246 families. No new runtime library or separate visualization module was introduced.

